@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .
@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .

<> a orexis:SelfGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO THIS AGENT IS: the courier, and this document is its own by the self it states. Booted as
#  "courier", the agent checks that this is so.
#
#  WHAT IT RUNS: it plans the route and walks it, in the packages' words, since the courier's domain
#  has none for an agent. Its world ships no rules, so it is no deliberator.

:courier a orexis:Self , planning:Planner , execution:Executor .

#  WHAT ITS SEARCH MAY SPEND IN A PASS, a stance (knowledge/domain/kernel/stance.md): the delivery
#  costs 45 candidates (measure-the-search), past planning's 32, so a pass at the constant publishes
#  nothing. `tests/test_courier.py` boots this world with no budget of its own and finds the plan in
#  one pass at this figure; at 32 it finds none.
:courier planning:budget 128 .
